extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market printed 154-161 and 190 (cache p155-p162 and p191, page_offset 1). Printed 154 introduces the Bio-Borgs, 155 is art, 156-157 hold the Player Note and the Bio-Borg Insanity Table, 157 the Partial Conversion rule and the opening of the True Bio-Borg R.C.C., 158-160 its creation steps (six orientations A-F, the Determination table of twelve bands, five augmentation tables of 14, 10, 7, 14 and 18 results), and 160-161 the shared stat block headed Partial & Full Bio-Borg R.C.C. Printed 159, 160, 161 and 190 read off 170 dpi renders on 2026-11-19; every figure below matches the render. The text layer sets 1D4x10+12 as !D4xlO+12 (cache p162), 5D6x10 as 5D6xlO and 1D6x10 as !D6xlO (cache p160). || NAME: id true-bio-borg; the book calls it the True Bio-Borg R.C.C. (also Elite or Full Bio-Borg). || GROUP: an R.C.C., played alone: men_of_arms false (an R.C.C. is a race), under the book''s heading The Bio-Borgs. The book prints its own R.C.C. related and secondary skills because the conversion replaces any past occupation, and they are stored here. || XP: printed 190, Experience Table for Full Conversion Bio-Borgs, lower bounds stored as printed (level 1 at 0). The Partial Conversion rule (157) says a Partial Bio-Borg uses the same table, so the partial variant shares it. || VARIANTS: full (the class-level bonuses, printed 161) and partial (+5D6 S.D.C., +1 P.S. and P.E., +1D4+1 Spd, +1 roll, +1 pull punch, +1 parry and dodge). The Mega-Damage alternatives (+4D6+4 M.D.C. full, +2D6+2 M.D.C. partial, in place of the S.D.C. bonus for a Mega-Damage creature) are conditional and not stored as bonuses. || ORIENTATIONS: a pick-one group of six; each orientation''s augmentation counts and skill grants are its description, not a mechanic. Orientation D stores I.Q. -1D6 and a P.S. floor of 40; its I.Q. maximum 10, Spd halved with maximum 12, Wrestling and the -5% to other skills are prose. Orientation E''s three additional ''other'' skills are read as three more R.C.C. related skills (related_skills_count 7). Orientation F''s lost secondary skills are prose. || DETERMINATION: a pick-one group of the twelve printed bands with a roll button; how many picks each band sends to each table is prose in the option, not enforced. || TABLES: each of the five augmentation tables is a pick group of up to three (the most any Determination band sends to one table); the dozen-feature cap, the G.M.''s 1-3 extra rolls, roll-again rows and incompatibilities are notes, not enforced. Numeric results are stored as option bonuses (S.D.C., P.S., P.E., P.P., Spd, combat) or an option mdc_base (the two M.D.C. Transformations, 75 and 120; an option base reads no per-level gain, so their +1D6 M.D.C. per level is prose and added by hand); healing rates, plate armor M.D.C., natural weapon damage, flight and supernatural P.S. are prose. Enhanced P.P. stores +4 and a P.P. floor of 22. || SPD 44: Table 5, 07-16 prints Enhanced Spd as +44; stored as +4 (Nate, 2026-11-18), the printed digits named in the option. || ORGANISMS: every parasite, symbiote and microbe a table names is named in its option as production''s gear row holds it (Living Armor (Parasite), Titanizer (Symbiote), Oplos (Parasite, mated pair), Chest Amalgamate (Chest Thing), Eye of Eylor (Bio-Wizard Eye) and the rest); none is granted as equipment. The Para-Juicer (Orientation F) has no row in this book or in production and stays prose. Dragon''s Fire Breath and Chemical Spray are Atlantis reconstructions and stay prose. || SKILLS: Language: Dragonese at 90 per_level 0; American is stored as Language: Native Tongue at 90 per_level 0, as the Atlantis imports store it. Body Building is the catalog''s Body Building & Weight Lifting. Hand to Hand: Expert, upgradable to Assassin or Martial Arts for one related pick each. Military excludes NBC Warfare, Parachuting and the three Demolitions rows; Piloting excludes robots, power armor, tanks and aircraft (the Tattooed Archer''s list); Technical excludes the computer skills; Cowboy, Medical and Pilot Related are None. || MONEY: None; stored as 0. An allowance of 2D4x10 credits a week for a trusted slave, and at most 1D6x100 stolen credits for a runaway, are prose. Slave market value 1D6x100,000 credits. || EQUIPMENT: one or two common weapons, clothing and personal items, plus light non-environmental body armor (30-50 M.D.C.) for a non-Mega-Damage Bio-Borg; too vague to grant, not stored. || NOT ROWS: the insanity table (156-157), the Partial Conversion rule (157), the insanity schedule (161) and the four deferred types (Bio-Leech, Fire Eater, Kill-Crazy, Sym-Killer, 161) are prose in the body, with no row."
